sequenceDiagram
  %% conn.environment_restart on the Gateway engine: the `Restart T3` step of conn/environment-restart.mmd (workflow operation-conn-environment-restart) as one `instance` family primitive. Design for ADR 0267 and ADR 0271; no engine flow exists yet. Step names describe effects; the implementation settles action names unless an existing action is named.
  %% Desired state: T3 answers with the machine name. A lost receipt never restarts T3 twice: the journal repeats the result, and a later send finds the label already right and restarts nothing.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: conn:environment-restart
  %% kind: conn.environment_restart
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane EN icon=workflow pill=engine tone=purple
  %% lane N icon=server pill=executor tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=copy tone=green
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant EN as Engine<br/>Gateway and NATS
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>executor
  participant C as Container<br/>via executor
  CLI->>GW: conn:environment-restart<br/>INSTANCE · or a Node's
  Note over GW: Read every T3 label<br/>at once · 5 s · no session
  %%> Same answers without an Operation as conn/environment-restart.mmd: skipped (frozen, stopped, no_t3, t3_unreadable) or current
  loop each candidate, by Instance ID
    Note over GW: Read its threads<br/>shell · admin session
    %%> The busy rule stays in the Gateway: a working run or pending runtime request answers `busy` `t3_working`; another Conn Operation `conn_operation`; at most four restarts a call, 120 s in all
    Note over GW: Admit the restart<br/>one Operation per Instance
    %%> The Operation holds the Instance's lock; its intent has no session
  end
  GW-->>CLI: 200 · one answer each<br/>restarting has operation_id
  alt the engine admits the whole Operation
    %%> Admission, one decision per Operation (EngineKinds::routes): `conn.environment_restart` is in `ORBIT_ENGINE_KINDS`, the Node reports the T3 restart action, and the flow accepts the plan, else `EngineUnsupported`
    EN->>C: Restart T3 when idle<br/>name · processes · restart
    %%> Answers `skipped` when the container no longer runs, `name_not_written` when /etc/machine-info lacks the name, `restarted` `already` when T3 already answers with the name
    %%> Right before the restart, reads T3's service members once: a terminal or command answers `busy` `processes` (unreadable: `processes_unreadable`) and restarts nothing
    %%> `systemctl try-restart t3.service`; nothing else restarts, the kernel hostname stays
    C-->>EN: Label read back<br/>restarted · window_ms
    %%> Readiness: reads the label on T3's port until it is the name, about 84 s at most; else `conn.t3_unready`, or `conn.t3_label_mismatch` for another label
    opt the receipt is lost
      EN->>C: Resend the same step<br/>fresh nonce · same step ID
      %%> When:
      %%> - the step passes its resend deadline with no receipt; two sends, one execution
      %%> - the Operation keeps its lock, so Instance 42 stays fenced; no other Operation and no Swamp run acts on it meanwhile
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - the journal holds `done` for this Operation step, action and target: the executor answers the stored result with `repeat: true` and does not act again
      %%> - an order still `open` replays under the target lock first; an order that expired before the lock did nothing (`executor.order_expired`), and the step is sent again
      C-->>EN: Stored result<br/>repeat: true
    end
    alt every step verified
      EN->>GW: Record the outcome<br/>restarted · busy · skipped
      %%> - the kind's own projection records the result, the same rows a Swamp run records
    else a step fails
      EN--xGW: Failed step<br/>error_code · redacted detail
      %%> - a deterministic refusal is a terminal receipt too; the journal keeps it and a resend repeats it
      Note over GW: Record the failure<br/>conn.t3_unready
      %%> - the Operation does not retry; a later call takes the Instance again
    end
  else the engine does not admit it
    Note over GW: Start the Swamp run<br/>operation-conn-environment-restart
    %%> - the kind is not enabled, a Node lacks the action, `$KV.NODES` is unreadable, or the flow throws `EngineUnsupported`: the whole Operation runs operation-conn-environment-restart (conn/environment-restart.mmd)
    %%> - no step of it runs on the engine; an Operation never splits across engines
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
